1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,500
That whine that gets louder in turns?

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,000
It's not your tires.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,500
A moaning or whining noise that changes pitch as you turn,

4
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,000
especially at low speed in a parking lot.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,500
That points to your differential—

6
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,000
the gears that let your wheels spin at different speeds in a turn.

7
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Low or worn-out gear oil lets those gears grind,

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
and the whine usually gets louder over time, not better.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,500
One clue is not a diagnosis—

10
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:26,000
worth having the differential fluid checked before it turns into a bigger repair.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,500
Stop by and we'll take a look—

12
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,000
Nick's Tire and Auto, on Euclid Avenue.

13
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
